# Who you are working with

Fill this in. An agent that knows what you are building, and who it is for, makes better
calls than one reasoning from the code alone. A few honest lines beat a long empty form.

**Name:**

**Role:** — what you do, and where you are strongest

**Project:** — what it is, and who uses it

**Why it matters:** — the outcome that makes the work worth doing

**Constraints:** — regulatory, contractual, performance, anything with real consequences

**How you work:** — where you want friction, where you do not. Corrections you have had to
make more than once belong here.
